  "body": "**Apply the quality-binding correction in #2984 before machine use or merge.** The following measurements describe the geometry on the tested control.\n\nStacked on #2992. Review the [convex tangent DXF changes above the parent](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/c81cfd1d44c0c210d5ba8ddc0fb1a63c3ac81342...feb802a77a99878951d5faf5ba2f41f65270c018).\n\nUse one complete, placed convex DXF loop of tangent lines and circular arcs as a Wire Contour punch. Keep the actual directed source segments. Check the emitted arc radii, tangencies, support line and complete stock envelope. A bounded, conservative preview runs through the normal workspace verification. The native writer keeps the nominal centers and arc sweeps.\n\nThe operator selects the placed profile, supplies an exterior threading point, and selects the supported captured punch process. Require a long enough supporting straight side for the entry and 1 mm separation. Folded, discontinuous or ill-conditioned loops and a rounding change that invalidates native tangency refuse before publication.\n\nRun the original examples:\n\n```sh\ncargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/rounded-punch.camscript\ncargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/three-corner-punch.camscript\n```\n\nAgie Control plotted the first job with four true corner arcs and alternating nominal radii of 4 and 6 mm. Their rough radii were 4.245 and 6.245 mm. The second job used three true circular sweeps of about 143.1301, 126.8699 and 90 degrees, plus an oblique straight side. Both jobs retained the 1.000 mm nominal separation. Each formal check had zero job errors and requested reference and machining setup. The control reported option 131072. No physical cut was made.\n\nThe independent gate passed 34 app tests, 18 native post tests and three geometry tests. Strict Clippy passed for the app, post and geometry libraries. The integrated branch reproduced both three-file jobs byte for byte. See #2984 for the separate safety correction to the binding of a resident quality.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: The Agie post preserves the nominal lines and arcs of a checked convex tangent DXF punch, including unequal corner radii and oblique sides.\n\nRefs #2022\nFixes #2983\n",
